 "post": {
  "title": "I Turned My Hobby Into a Side Hustle for 6 Weeks #shorts",
  "description": "Which hobby did you turn into a job? Tell me in the comments. Send this to the friend who monetized their joy. Your hobby is drawing, just for fun. Then you start selling it, and six weeks later you don't touch the pen on a free Sunday. In 'Undermining Children's Intrinsic Interest with Extrinsic Reward: A Test of the Overjustification Hypothesis' (Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, 1973), Mark Lepper, David Greene and Richard Nisbett promised preschoolers who already liked drawing a 'Good Player' certificate with a gold seal and ribbon. Later, in free play, those kids spent about half as much time drawing (about 9% vs 17-18%) as kids who got no reward or an unexpected one. The reward became the reason. Keep one thing unpaid. #psychology #shorts #sidehustle #motivation #overthinking",
  "tags": [
   "overjustification effect",
   "side hustle",
   "intrinsic motivation",
   "Lepper Greene Nisbett",
   "psychology"
  ]
 },
